      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So basically it's just like Depth of Field? And if so then a huge NO as that would be horrible in a VR experience.\n\nThe only way something like this would be usable is if everyone had the same VR technology that allowed their eyes to be tracked so you can tell what the user is focusing on. Because even if you don't move your head, you can still move your eyes and focus on things closer or further away. But it would have to update super fast and I don't think anyone can do it. Even if done right it's just going to be disorienting and make people sick.\n\nI myself go insane if there is any blur when I am in VR and it makes me think my lens are dirty.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
